Feed anticoccidials are specialized additives incorporated into animal feed to prevent and control coccidiosis, a parasitic disease that can affect poultry and other livestock. These products help maintain animal health, support productivity, and reduce the impact of infections on commercial farming operations.

The market includes synthetic compounds, such as ionophores and chemical anticoccidials, alongside emerging natural alternatives. Demand is closely linked to commercial poultry production, livestock disease management, feed manufacturing practices, and food safety requirements. Manufacturers are also working to address concerns around resistance and changing regulations through new formulations and alternative approaches.

